  {"id":"fivePillars.zakah.summary","source":"components/learning/FivePillarsVisual.tsx","english":"A defined annual percentage (usually 2.5%) paid by eligible Muslims to support the poor and needy.","arabic_source":"مقدار محدد شرعًا من المال الفائض عن النصاب يُعطى للفقراء والمستحقين.","french":"Une part annuelle déterminée (généralement 2,5 %) versée par les musulmans qui remplissent les conditions afin de soutenir les pauvres et les personnes dans le besoin.","source_refs":["Bukhari 1395"],"status":"needs-mo-review","hold_reason":"The mapped source only supports obligatory giving from wealth and distribution to the poor; the flat 2.5% figure and its conditions need an identified source before this copy can be used."},
